course: dictionary
lesson: 3028
title: Eagle: a bird of prey
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eagle is a large, strong bird. The sentence «Eagles are big birds of prey: hunters with hooked beaks, huge feet and amazing eyes» gives you clues. Hunters, hooked beaks and huge feet tell you that an eagle catches and eats other animals.
explain: The phrase «an eagle swoops down with a fierce scream» is another clue. Swoops means it drops fast from the sky, and fierce means it is strong and wild. So an eagle is a bird that hunts from the air.
explain: Words can also have a second meaning. In golf, an eagle is a score, not a bird. You can tell which meaning is used by reading the words around it: a golf course and a score point to golf, while a nest and a scream point to the bird.
fact: An eagle is a large, strong bird of prey with a hooked beak, sharp claws called talons, and excellent eyesight.
fact: A bird of prey is a bird that hunts and eats other animals.
fact: In golf, an eagle is a score of two shots less than par for a hole.
fact: The bald eagle is the national bird of the USA, and the wedge-tailed eagle lives in Australia.
fact: An eagle's nest is called an eyrie. «Eagle-eyed» means having very sharp eyesight, so you notice small things.
exercise: «Eagles are big birds of prey: hunters with hooked beaks, huge feet and amazing eyes.» What is a bird of prey? | A bird that sings loudly at dawn | A bird that cannot fly | A bird that lives only in water | *A bird that hunts and eats other animals
exercise: In golf, what is an eagle? | A bird that lives on the golf course | *A score of two shots less than par for a hole | A score of two shots more than par | A kind of golf club
exercise: «In a nature film a tiny ant marches across a leaf, and an eagle swoops down with a fierce scream.» Find and copy one word that tells you the eagle moves fast through the air. | *swoops | marches | tiny | leaf
test: What does «eagle-eyed» suggest about a person? | *Very sharp eyesight, noticing small things | Good at singing | Afraid of birds | Very slow and clumsy
test: Which bird is the national bird of the USA? | Wedge-tailed eagle | Parrot | *Bald eagle | Robin
exam: Which phrase means an eagle's nest? | golden eagle | *eyrie | eagle-eyed | talon
